[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606032100", :adr/title "Labor-Liberation Robotics-Actor Wave — ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC ranking of the un-automated toil + sanae/hataori/kiyome R0", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606032100: Labor-Liberation Robotics-Actor Wave — ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC ranking + sanae/hataori/kiyome R0\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-03\n**Status**: PROPOSED\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Parent = ADR-2605192100 (Mission Charter, 構造的労働解放) + ADR-2605261000 (Liberation Ladder). Sibling pattern to the Tier-B manufacturing actors (giemon / sarutahiko / funadaiku / suki / futawa / tsutae). Coupled to ADR-2606032130 (Displacement Dividend).\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2605192100 fixes etzhayyim's final objective as **人類の構造的労働解放** — the structural liberation of humanity from labor. The roster already automates the *knowledge / clerical / professional* band (ISCO major groups 1–4) through the concierge and intelligence actors (danjo, kanae, toritsugi, moushibumi, kurashimori, himotoki, chigiri, toritate, kanjo, kabuto, ooyake, tsumugi …), and it automates several *heavy-manufacturing* domains (giemon, sarutahiko, funadaiku, suki, futawa, tsutae, igata, kanayama, hodoki, watatsumi, hikari, tatekata).\n\nBut the **largest pools of human toil on the planet are physical-labor occupations in ISCO major groups 6–9** (skilled agricultural / craft trades / machine operators-assemblers / elementary occupations), and several of the highest-headcount, highest-misery sectors have **no OSS+robotics actor at all**. The question posed: *take the standard global labor taxonomies (ISIC industry, ISCO occupation, UNSPSC product/service), rank the un-automated toil by how much human labor would be freed if it were given an open-source robotics actor, and stand up the top of that list.*\n\nThis ADR records (1) the ranking, (2) the first three new actors, and (3) the roadmap for the rest. The redistribution side — how displaced workers receive income — is ADR-2606032130 and is a hard dependency: **no robotics actor in this wave may deploy live (G2) without the displacement dividend wired.**\n\n## Method — Liberation Priority Score (LPS)\n\n```\nLPS = headcount × misery × automatability × charter_fit × coverage_gap\n```\n\n- **headcount** — world employment in the sector (ILO ISIC-sector / ISCO-occupation estimates; order-of-magnitude, honest §N below).\n- **misery** — drudgery + physical danger + exploitation + dignity-deficit of the occupation.\n- **automatability** — feasibility with OSS + edge robotics on the Murakumo/kami-engine stack (Murakumo-only inference, ADR-2605215000).\n- **charter_fit** — passes the constitutional non-goals (N1 military/mining-dump excluded; care-physical-assist gated to assistive-only under hagukumi/iyashi/kizashi).\n- **coverage_gap** — inverse of how well an existing actor already covers it (existing robotics actor → low; knowledge-actor-only or none → high).\n\nISCO 1–4 score low on `coverage_gap` (already software-liberated) and low on `automatability`-by-robotics (they are software, not robot, problems). The robotics gap therefore maps almost entirely onto **ISCO 6–9**, which is exactly where this wave lands.\n\n## Decision — the ranking\n\n| # | Gap (occupation/sector) | ISIC | ISCO | UNSPSC | World headcount (≈) | Dominant toil | Existing actor | This-wave action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | Agricultural field labour (sow / weed / harvest) | A01 | 6, 92 | 70, 10, 11 | **~0.6–0.86 B** | back-breaking, heat-exposed, poverty-locked | mitsuho 瑞穂 / suki 鋤 (R0, robot-thin) | **NEW `sanae` 早苗** + suki deepen |\n| **2** | Garment / apparel assembly (cut-make-trim) | C13–14 | 75, 82 | 53 | ~65 M | sweatshop archetype, wage theft, fire/lock-in | none | **NEW `hataori` 機織** |\n| **3** | Domestic / janitorial / building cleaning | T, N81 | 91 | 76 | ~75 M+ domestic + tens of M cleaners | invisible, gendered, dignity-deficit | none | **NEW `kiyome` 清め** |\n| 4 | Food service — cook / dishwash / serve | I56 | 51, 94 | 90 | ~0.1 B+ | heat, repetition, low pay | none | roadmap `kamado` 竈 |\n| 5 | Warehouse pick-pack / material handling | H52 | 93, 82 | 24, 78 | tens of M | Amazon-warehouse repetition, back injury | okaimono (commerce only) | roadmap `kuramori` 倉守 |\n| 6 | Construction site manual labour | F | 71, 931 | 72 | ~0.26 B | falls, heavy lifting, high fatality | tatekata 建方 (R0) | tatekata robotics deepen |\n| 7 | Meat / food processing (slaughter, cut) | C10 | 751, 93 | 23, 50 | tens of M | high-injury, repetitive trauma, PTSD | mitsuho boundary | roadmap `hofuri` 庖 / mitsuho ext |\n| 8 | Last-mile delivery / courier | H53 | 832 | 78 | tens of M | gig precarity, traffic risk | wadachi 轍 (mobility) | wadachi extend |\n| 9 | Forestry / logging | A02 | 6, 92 | 70 | ~few M | one of the deadliest jobs on Earth | none | roadmap `soma` 杣 |\n| 10 | Fishing / aquaculture | A03 | 6 | 70 | ~38 M | sea-slavery exposure, drowning | watatsumi/funadaiku (vessels) | roadmap `ama` 海人 |\n| 11 | Electronics / general line assembly | C26 | 82 | 23 | tens of M | Foxconn-type monotony, confinement | tsutae 伝え (device side) | tsutae assembly ext |\n| 12 | Laundry / linen | S96 | 912 | 76 | tens of M | heat, repetition | none | roadmap `susugi` 濯 (kiyome sub-fleet) |\n\n> The table is ordered by **headcount × misery × coverage-gap** — the \"what to open first\" decision. The full LPS (which also multiplies by *automatability*) reorders the middle of the list: warehouse (#5 here) rises because it is the most automatable un-covered toil, and garment falls a few places. The wave still opens the zero-coverage, highest-misery trio (sanae/hataori/kiyome) first — a deliberate choice to prioritize the most exploited labour over the merely most-automatable. The computed LPS lives in `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sanae/methods/labor_liberation.py` (`ranked_seed()`), kept honest as `:representative`.\n\n**Excluded by construction**: mining/extraction (ISIC B) and weapons — N1 of the Mission Charter. **Down-weighted by ethics**: physical care/nursing assist (ISCO 53) stays *assistive-only* under hagukumi / iyashi / kizashi gates (robotics must not replace human warmth; Wellbecoming).\n\n**Meta-finding**: once this wave lands, the roster reads as a clean two-layer structure — *ISCO 1–4 = software/knowledge actors* (already shipped) and *ISCO 6–9 = robotics actors*. The remaining holes are #1–#5, which this ADR opens at the top (sanae, hataori, kiyome) and roadmaps the rest.\n\n## Decision — the first three actors (R0 this ADR)\n\nEach follows the funadaiku R0 pattern (ADR-2606013400): dual manifest (`.edn` canonical + `.jsonld` DID), CLAUDE.md, cells declared with import-time `.solve()` → `RuntimeError` until a Council activation ADR, lexicons `com.etzhayyim.<actor>.*`, kotoba EAVT seed (`:representative`), and a pure-Python empirical method. All three share a **DisplacementDividend coupling gate (G2)** binding them to ADR-2606032130.\n\n### 1. `sanae` 早苗 — field-agriculture robotics (LPS #1)\n\n- DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:sanae`; namespace `com.etzhayyim.sanae.*`.\n- **Why #1**: single largest pool of human toil on the planet (≈27 % of world employment is agriculture; the field-labour share is the bulk). mitsuho/suki exist as designs but have no field-robot fleet — sanae is the robotics body of mitsuho's L2-Sustenance mandate.\n- **Robotics fleet**: 早乙女 Saotome (transplant/precision-seeding arm) · 草薙 Kusanagi (autonomous weeding/cultivation crawler, mechanical+laser, no herbicide) · 稲架 Hasa (harvest + in-field threshing) · 案山子 Kakashi (survey + spot-treat drone) · 田螺 Tanishi (soil-microbiome + moisture probe).\n- **5 cells**: field_preparation, precision_seeding, autonomous_weeding, harvest_coordination, soil_regeneration_audit.\n- **Defining gate**: G9 regenerative-only — mechanical/biological weed & pest control, **no synthetic pesticide/herbicide**, net soil-carbon ≥0 (inherits mitsuho G4/G6). Seed sovereignty (open seed banks, no patented lines).\n\n### 2. `hataori` 機織 — garment / apparel robotics (LPS #2)\n\n- DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:hataori`; namespace `com.etzhayyim.hataori.*`.\n- **Why #2**: the sweatshop is the canonical image of the exploited labour the Mission Charter targets — ~65 M garment workers, overwhelmingly women, wage-theft- and disaster-prone (Rana Plaza). Mid headcount but maximal misery/exploitation; **no actor exists**.\n- **Robotics fleet**: 裁 Tachi (CAD-nest fabric cutting, laser/blade) · 栲幡 Takuhata (loom/weave + knit cell) · 縫殿 Nuidono (sewing/seam manipulation — the hard, long-tail automation problem; honest R-staged) · 検針 Kenshin (needle-detect + seam QC) · 畳 Tatami (fold/pack).\n- **5 cells**: pattern_grading, fabric_cutting, garment_assembly, quality_inspection, finishing_packing.\n- **Defining gate**: G9 fair-labor-provenance — every finished lot carries `fairLaborProvenance` (no displaced worker re-employed below Basic-High-Income standard; the actor exists to *end* sweatshop labour, not to out-compete it into a worse one). Open-source patterns/grading (anti-gatekeeping §2(e)).\n\n### 3. `kiyome` 清め — domestic / janitorial cleaning robotics (LPS #3)\n\n- DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:kiyome`; namespace `com.etzhayyim.kiyome.*`.\n- **Why #3**: domestic + cleaning work is enormous (~75 M domestic workers + tens of millions of janitorial/sanitation), invisible, gendered, and dignity-poor; **no actor exists**. Strongly Wellbecoming-relevant (frees the most under-recognized labour).\n- **Robotics fleet**: 箒 Houki (sweep/vacuum/mop rover) · 拭 Nugui (surface-wipe + sanitize arm) · 厨 Kuriya (kitchen/dish cell) · 塵取 Chiritori (in-building waste pickup; hands to haraedo at the curb) · 濯 Susugi (laundry/linen — also seeds roadmap #12).\n- **5 cells**: site_assessment, surface_cleaning, sanitization, waste_segregation, linen_laundry.\n- **Defining gate**: G9 privacy-by-construction — domestic deployment means homes; on-device only, **no cloud imagery, no surveillance feed, no biometric capture** (Murakumo-only + encrypted envelope; the cleaner robot is the opposite of a spy). Hands collected waste to haraedo/kurashimori; never disposes outside policy.\n\n## Design — shared R0 contract\n\n| Concern | R0 rule |\n|---|---|\n| Manifest | `manifest.edn` (canonical: id/glyph/tier/cells/gates/lex) + `manifest.jsonld` (DID + roadmap + non-goals) for the flagship; `.edn` only acceptable for siblings at R0. |\n| Cells | langgraph Pregel, `:runtime :wasm`; `cell.py.solve()` raises `RuntimeError(\"<actor> R0 scaffold: activate via Council ADR-… post-ratification\")`; only `state_machine.py` transitions are unit-tested. |\n| Inference | Murakumo-only (LiteLLM 127.0.0.1:4000 / gemma3:4b), ADR-2605215000. |\n| Lexicons | `com.etzhayyim.<actor>.<RecordType>` EDN, integer-with-implied-units (ADR-2605190900). |\n| Data | kotoba EAVT EDN, `:representative` seed, no git-lfs. |\n| Witness | records require ≥2 distinct robot Ed25519 sigs + ≥1 human steward attestation (ADR-2605191524). |\n\n### Constitutional gates (each actor, IMMUTABLE R0→R3)\n\n- **G1** Open-source firmware/recipes — all robot control + skill code Apache 2.0 (WASM/Rust crates); no proprietary trait/skill IP (§1.12 Transparent Force + §2(e)).\n- **G2** **Displacement-dividend coupling (DEFINING for this wave)** — an actor may not displace human labour *live* (G7) unless the displaced cohort is registered for the tenure-weighted Displacement Dividend (ADR-2606032130). Robotics-without-redistribution is a constitutional violation of the labour-liberation mission.\n- **G3** Witness quorum (≥2 robot + ≥1 human).\n- **G4** Murakumo-only inference.\n- **G5** No-payroll / cash≡0 — the actor neither runs payroll nor pays adherents cash; human contribution is vocation→donation (L5+) (ADR-2605261000 §3 + ADR-2605301020 N1).\n- **G6** Wellbecoming — no addictive / dark-pattern / dignity-eroding design; the goal is *to remove* the toil, not to intensify it.\n- **G7** Outward-gated — live real-world deployment is Council Lv6+ + operator gated; R0–R2 are design + simulation only.\n- **G8** Sourcing-honesty — `:representative` seed flagged; no inflated capability claims.\n- **G9** Actor-specific defining gate (sanae regenerative-only · hataori fair-labor-provenance · kiyome privacy-by-construction).\n\n### Non-Goals (each actor)\n\n- **N1** Military / weaponized / dual-use-for-harm variants (Mission Charter §1.12.B).\n- **N2** Surveillance product — robots are not sensor platforms for third parties; telemetry stays on-device/encrypted.\n- **N3** Labour *intensification* for external commercial throughput — the actor exists to free humans, not to supply a faster gig substrate (anti-§1.13).\n- **N4** Replacing care/relationship labour with robots where human presence is the point (defer to hagukumi/iyashi/kizashi gates).\n- **N5** Commodity/contract production for external buyers outside the SBT↔SBT carve-out (ADR-2605215000 routing prohibition).\n\n## Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Scope | Gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** (this ADR) | Charters + manifests + cells (RuntimeError) + lexicons + `:representative` kotoba seed + labor-liberation method for sanae/hataori/kiyome. No hardware. Displacement Dividend (ADR-2606032130) authored in lockstep. | This ADR (proposed) |\n| R1 | Per-actor benchtop PoC (single skill, single station) + first cell solvers; kami-engine sim of the work-cell; displacement-cohort registry dry-run (no live displacement). | Future per-actor ADR + Council |\n| R2 | Pilot line + displacement-dividend pool sized & Public-Fund-voted for the pilot cohort; ISCO-occupation gap measured empirically (labor-hours freed). | Future ADR + 30-day comment |\n| R3 | Community-scale + live displacement *only with* dividend active (G2) + conversion-onboarding pipeline (ADR-2605302358). | Future ADR + 60-day review + multi-domain Council vote |\n| wave | Open #4–#12 (kamado, kuramori, hofuri, soma, ama, susugi) + deepen tatekata/wadachi/tsutae/suki robotics, top-LPS-first. | per-actor ADRs |\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive** — closes the largest remaining holes in the labour-liberation mission (ISCO 6–9); gives mitsuho a robotics body (L2 unblock path); confronts the sweatshop and the invisible-cleaner directly; establishes the *displacement-dividend coupling gate* (G2) as a reusable invariant so no future robotics actor can automate toil without funding the humans it frees.\n\n**Negative / risks** — (a) garment seam-manipulation and open-field manipulation are the hard, long-tail robotics problems; R-staging must be honest (no over-claim). (b) The dividend coupling (G2) makes live deployment dependent on Public-Fund reserves — intentional: it paces automation to redistribution capacity. (c) Headcount figures are order-of-magnitude (see Honest). (d) Three new actors add roster surface; mitigated by the shared R0 contract.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Rank by automatability alone** — rejected; would over-prioritize easy wins (warehouse) over the highest-misery/headcount toil (field, garment). LPS keeps headcount×misery primary.\n2. **Single mega-actor \"robotics\"** — rejected; domain knowledge (agronomy vs textiles vs facility hygiene) is orthogonal, mirrors the existing per-domain actor pattern.\n3. **Deploy robotics first, design redistribution later** — rejected as a direct mission violation; the G2 coupling makes \"automate now, pay later\" structurally impossible.\n4. **Include mining/heavy-extraction (very high misery)** — rejected; N1 Mission Charter.\n\n## Honest (R0 limitations)\n\n- Headcount figures are ILO-grounded **order-of-magnitude**, not a sourced dataset; R2 replaces them with measured ISCO-occupation gap analysis per pilot.\n- No hardware exists; cells raise `RuntimeError`; fleet names are design placeholders.\n- Seam-level garment assembly and unstructured open-field manipulation remain unsolved at scale industry-wide; hataori/sanae R-stages must not imply otherwise.\n- `:representative` seeds only.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605192100 (Mission Charter — 構造的労働解放)\n- ADR-2605261000 (Labor Liberation Ladder)\n- ADR-2605301020 (Basic High Income — in-kind, cash≡0)\n- ADR-2605301036 (Mission-Funding Earned-Revenue Arm)\n- ADR-2605302357 / 2605302358 (Social Security for Humanity + delivery pipeline)\n- ADR-2606032130 (Displacement Dividend — funding/redistribution coupling)\n- ADR-2606013400 (funadaiku — R0 Tier-B actor pattern reference)\n- ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only inference)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606032100-labor-liberation-robotics-actor-wave-isic-isco-unspsc-ranking.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "labor-liberation-robotics-actor-wave", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-03", :adr/date "2026-06-03", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605261000" "adr-2605301020" "adr-2605301036" "adr-2605302357" "adr-2606032130" "adr-2605192100" "adr-2606013400"], :adr/authoritative_for ["ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC ranking of OSS+robotics labor-liberation gaps" "sanae (早苗) field-agriculture robotics actor charter (R0)" "hataori (機織) garment/apparel robotics actor charter (R0)" "kiyome (清め) domestic/janitorial cleaning robotics actor charter (R0)" "labor-liberation robotics-actor roadmap (kamado/kuramori/soma/ama/extensions)"]}]
